<title>USA: Lockheed Martin gets $1.59 bln contract.</title>
<headline>Lockheed Martin gets $1.59 bln contract.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Lockheed Martin Missiles and Space division of Lockheed Martin Corp has received a $1.59 billion U.S. defense contract for development of a satellite system to detect missile launches, the Air Force said.</p>
<p>The contract is for development and delivery of five geosynchronous satellites with infra-red detection capability and a ground system as well as two special payloads, the Air Force said.</p>
<p>Work on the satellites and other equipment is expected to be completed in the year 2006.</p>
</text>
